Shows the event types, which the objects in your simulation model schedule during the simulation, and
which the EventController then processes.
Remarks
Plant Simulation provides these types of simulation events:
Event English Event German Action taking place/state of the object
* * Designates any type of event.
Animation Animation A MU is located on a Track, Conveyor, or on a Buffer.
Battery Batterie The battery of a Transporter is full, empty or on reserve.
BlockageEnd BlockierEnde The state of a MU changes to unblocked.
Bump Anstoss The Transporter collides with another MU. You can then take
appropriate actions in the Collision control.
CheckMUDistance BEAbstandPrüfen The MU distance at the start of the Conveyor is reached;
if Enforce MU distance is activated, the MU has reached the
distance to the part moving in front.
CheckMUPosition BEPositionPrüfen Checks if the MU has to be stopped after processing the exit
control on length-oriented objects. This is the case if neither
the position of the front in the direction of motion nor the
direction changed.
CreateMU ErzeugeBE The Source attempts to create MUs.
DeliverParts TeileAbliefern The Worker picked up parts at a station and carries them to
the destination object.
DisruptionBegin StörBeginn The failure of the object starts.
