Real-time x [EventController]
Select the real-time scaling factor. Depending on the simulation control button you click, Plant
Simulation uses different real-time scaling factors.
Remarks
Note
Normally Plant Simulation does not take the time span between events into account, as it is a discrete
event simulation system.
You can type in or select a scaling factor for the different settings. The scaling factor sets the time that
elapses between two events in real-time. The duration of an event in real-time is the simulation time
divided by the scaling factor you entered. The resulting duration is an integer value.
• When you click Start/Stop Simulation, Plant Simulation uses real-time simulation with a scaling factor
of 3 by default.
• When you click Start Full Speed Simulation, Plant Simulation ignores the scaling factor. This starts the
simulation run with the animation of MUs and States 
  and with full speed.
• When you click Start Fast Forward Simulation, Plant Simulation ignores the scaling factor. This starts
the simulation run without the animation of MUs and States 
  and with maximum speed.
Real-time x [EventController]
