11-1344 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Skip Long Event Intervals
To skip long phases during which no relevant event takes place during real-time simulation, select this
check box.
Remarks
Events of type Animation and UpdateDisplay are considered to be not relevant.
The simulation fast forwards the gap between events if no relevant event would take place for at least 10
seconds, while the animation remains active. These 10 seconds are 10 seconds in real-time which you
would have to wait for. For a real-time scaling factor of 3 this would amount to 30 seconds of simulation
time. Fast forwarding starts about half a second after the last event and ends about half a second before
the next event.
The open windows of the simulation show the Fast Forward Simulation icon during this time. The icon
looks like this:
This setting is especially helpful for simulation models in which you experiment with different Shifts.
