Condition [breakpoint]
Type in any Condition you would like to apply to the definition of the breakpoint. Before an event is
released for execution, the Event Debugger checks the expression you entered.
Remarks
This specified expression may be anything that returns a boolean value. If the condition returns true, the
Event Debugger stops the simulation. If you use a formula for the Condition, you can access the Receiver
using the anonymous identifier @. You might, for example, enter @.Name = "Wheel" AND @.getNo =
4 or @.length<100
The anonymous identifier ? accesses the Sender of the event.
Or click 
  and select a Method in the dialog Select Object.
Note
The Method Debugger cannot track the method of the condition!
See also
Select Object
EventDebugger Example 4
Condition [breakpoint]
